{#- Sentinel Arena evaluation report (Stage 7 #17; Jinja2 autoescape, D57 structure).
    FROZEN: analyst/render.py records this file's sha256 in every report; a test checks it.
    One template, two views: the brief (brief=True: decision required, executive summary,
    options, decision criteria, decision record) and the full report.
    AI text arrives only as segments: "text" is autoescaped, "fig" is code-formatted. -#}
{%- macro prose(segs) -%}
{%- for s in segs -%}
{%- if s.t == "fig" -%}<span class="fig c-{{ s.confidence|lower }}" title="{{ s.label }} · confidence {{ s.confidence }}">{{ s.s }}</span>
{%- else -%}{{ s.s }}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro by(who) -%}<span class="by by-{{ who|lower }}">written by {{ who }}</span>{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro options_table() -%}
<table>
  <tr><th>Option</th><th>Summary</th><th>Strengths</th><th>Weaknesses</th></tr>
  {% for o in options %}
  <tr><td><b>{{ o.id }}</b></td><td>{{ prose(o.summary) }}</td>
    <td><ul>{% for s in o.strengths %}<li>{{ prose(s) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></td>
    <td><ul>{% for s in o.weaknesses %}<li>{{ prose(s) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro criteria_table() -%}
<table>
  <tr><th>If you value…</th><th>Option</th><th>Because</th></tr>
  {% for c in criteria %}
  <tr><td>{{ prose(c.value) }}</td><td><b>{{ c.option }}</b></td><td>{{ prose(c.because) }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro decision_record() -%}
<table class="decision">
  <tr><th>Decision: option A, B or C (or none)</th><td></td></tr>
  <tr><th>The decision-maker's criterion (from the decision criteria)</th><td></td></tr>
  <tr><th>Decided by</th><td></td></tr>
  <tr><th>Date</th><td></td></tr>
</table>
<p class="muted">Completed by the decision-maker, not by the AI. In the demo the presenter acts as decision-maker, states the option and the criterion behind it, and fills in this record.</p>
{%- endmacro -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:">
<title>Sentinel Arena — {{ "decision brief" if brief else "evaluation report" }}</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink:#111827; --muted:#4b5563; --line:#d1d5db; --high:#065f46; --moderate:#92400e; --low:#991b1b; }
  body { font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: var(--ink); background:#fff; max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 24px; }
  h1 { font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 4px; } h2 { font-size: 20px; margin: 28px 0 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-bottom: 4px; }
  h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 18px 0 6px; } p { margin: 6px 0; } .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .by { float: right; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); }
  .by-ai { background:#eef2ff; color:#3730a3; border-color:#c7d2fe; } .by-code { background:#f3f4f6; } .by-human { background:#fef3c7; color:#92400e; border-color:#fde68a; }
  .fig { font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 2px solid; }
  .c-high { border-color: var(--high); } .c-moderate { border-color: var(--moderate); } .c-low { border-color: var(--low); }
  .conf { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #fff; white-space: nowrap; }
  .conf-high { background: var(--high); } .conf-moderate { background: var(--moderate); } .conf-low { background: var(--low); }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 13px; margin: 8px 0; } th, td { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 4px 6px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f3f4f6; } code { font-size: 12px; } ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; }
  .finding { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; margin: 10px 0; }
  .box { border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; margin: 12px 0; }
  .decide { border: 3px solid var(--ink); background: #f9fafb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; }
  .decision td { height: 30px; } .decision th { width: 45%; }
  .legend { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
  .legend .by { float: none; }
  @media print {
    body { max-width: none; padding: 0; font-size: 10.5pt; }
    .appendix { break-before: page; }
    .finding, .box, .decide, tr { break-inside: avoid; }
    @page { size: A4; margin: 16mm 15mm; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{% if brief %}
<h1>Sentinel Arena — decision brief</h1>
<p class="muted">AI defender evaluation · {{ meta.date }} · prose drafted by an AI analyst ({{ meta.model }}); every number filled in by code; the decision is made by a person. Full report: {{ meta.report_id }}.</p>
<div class="decide">Decision required: choose option A, B or C.</div>
<p class="legend">Each underlined figure carries a confidence level set by pre-registered rules (green High, amber Moderate, red Low); the full report gives every rate's 95% interval. The executive summary, options and decision criteria are {{ by("AI") }}; the decision record is completed by a person.</p>

<h2>Executive summary</h2>
<p>{{ prose(sections.executive_summary) }}</p>

<h2>Options</h2>
{{ options_table() }}

<h2>Decision criteria</h2>
{{ criteria_table() }}

<h2>Decision record {{ by("human") }}</h2>
{{ decision_record() }}
<p class="muted">The analyst never recommends an option. Sources, methods, all findings with their confidence, limitations and the evidence manifest are in the full report.</p>
{% else %}
<h1>Sentinel Arena — evaluation report</h1>
<p class="muted">AI defender evaluation · {{ meta.report_id }} · {{ meta.date }} · prose drafted by an AI analyst ({{ meta.model }}); every number filled in by code; the decision is made by a person.</p>

<h2>0. Document control {{ by("code") }}</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Report</th><td>{{ meta.report_id }} (report format {{ report_version }})</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Evidence summary</th><td>built {{ summary.built_at }} from frozen evidence (summary format {{ summary.schema_version }}, code version <code>{{ ((summary.git or {}).get("commit") or "—")[:12] }}</code>)</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Analyst</th><td>{{ meta.model }} ({{ meta.provider }}), prompt v{{ meta.prompt_version }}, {{ meta.attempts }} attempt(s), cost {{ meta.cost_usd|usd_appendix }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Grounding check</th><td>{{ "passed" if ground.ok else "FAILED" }}: every figure placeholder and reference checked by code</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Status</th><td>Draft for human review. The decision record (section 10) is completed by the decision-maker, not by the AI.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>1. Executive summary {{ by("AI") }}</h2>
<div class="decide">Decision required: choose option A, B or C.</div>
<p>{{ prose(sections.executive_summary) }}</p>

<h2>2. Scope {{ by("code") }}</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Experiment</th><th>Defender</th><th>Matches</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
  {% for g in summary.groups %}
  <tr><td>{{ g.label }}</td><td>{{ {"original": "default defender", "open": "open-definition defender"}.get(g.blue, "—") }}</td><td>{{ g.folders }}</td><td>{{ g.notes|join("; ") or "—" }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>3. Methodology {{ by("AI") }}</h2>
<p>{{ prose(sections.methodology) }}</p>
<p class="muted">Fixed facts (code): Red attacks a test web application through a logging proxy; Blue reads only the proxy log after the traffic, so it detects, it does not block; a deterministic Judge scores each round. Confidence levels follow rules fixed before any result was summarised: checked figures (attack labels checked by the designer, or normal requests known by construction) with at least twenty units are High, fewer are Moderate; unchecked attack labels are Low; the open-definition defender is capped at Moderate. See the glossary.</p>

<h2>4. Results {{ by("code") }}</h2>
<p>{{ prose(sections.results) }} <span class="by by-ai">narrative by AI</span></p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Figure</th><th>Value</th><th>95% interval</th><th>Units</th><th>Confidence</th><th>What it counts</th></tr>
  {% for r in results %}{% if r.key in cited %}
  <tr><td>{{ r.f.label }}</td><td>{{ r.text }}</td><td>{{ r.ci or "—" }}</td><td>{{ r.f.n }} {{ r.f.unit }}</td><td><span class="conf conf-{{ r.f.confidence|lower }}">{{ r.f.confidence }}</span></td><td>{{ r.f.definition }}</td></tr>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>5. Key findings {{ by("AI") }}</h2>
<p class="muted">Finding text by the AI; each finding's confidence is set by code: the lowest among the figures it cites.</p>
{% for f in findings %}
<div class="finding">
  <h3>{{ f.id }} · {{ prose(f.title) }} <span class="conf conf-{{ (f.confidence or "low")|lower }}">{{ f.confidence or "—" }}</span></h3>
  <p>{{ prose(f.text) }}</p>
  <p class="muted">Figures: {{ f.figure_labels|join("; ") }}. Evidence: {{ f.evidence_labels|join("; ") }} (Appendix A).</p>
</div>
{% endfor %}

<h2>6. Risk register {{ by("AI") }}</h2>
<p>{{ prose(sections.risk_register) }}</p>

<h2>7. Deployment options {{ by("AI") }}</h2>
<p>{{ prose(sections.deployment_options) }}</p>
{{ options_table() }}

<h2>8. Decision criteria {{ by("AI") }}</h2>
<p>{{ prose(sections.decision_criteria) }}</p>
{{ criteria_table() }}

<h2>9. Limitations {{ by("AI") }}</h2>
<p>{{ prose(sections.limitations) }}</p>
<div class="box"><b>Fixed disclosures (code).</b>
  <ul>
    <li>The free-play attack attempts were judged by the designer after the open-definition defender's results were known.</li>
    <li>The open-definition defender's verdicts vary run to run; its figures are capped at Moderate.</li>
    <li>The twenty-unit confidence threshold was set knowing the sample sizes; it puts the free-play detection figures at Moderate, against our own headline result.</li>
    <li>Added after the first draft (post hoc): a finding may not mix figures from unchecked attack labels with checked figures, so a checked result is not rated by its unchecked contrast.</li>
    {% if meta.provider == "openai" %}<li>The evidence includes an OpenAI attacker (gpt-6-luna); an OpenAI analyst model commenting on it is disclosed here.</li>
    {% elif meta.provider == "anthropic" %}<li>The analyst model is from the same family as the defender (Anthropic); disclosed here.</li>
    {% else %}<li>Analyst provider: {{ meta.provider }}.</li>{% endif %}
    <li>The analyst never recommends an option; the decision is made by a person.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>10. Decision record {{ by("human") }}</h2>
{{ decision_record() }}

<h2 class="appendix">Appendix A. Evidence manifest {{ by("code") }}</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Source</th><th>Experiment</th><th>Path</th><th>Match</th><th>Artifacts (sha256)</th></tr>
  {% for s in summary.sources %}
  <tr><td><code>{{ s.id }}</code></td><td>{{ group_label.get(s.id.split("#")[0], "") }}</td><td><code>{{ s.path }}</code></td><td><code>{{ s.match_id or "—" }}</code></td>
    <td>{% for a in s.artifacts %}<code>{{ a.file }} {{ a.sha256[:12] }}</code>{{ "; " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>Appendix B. AI disclosure and identifiers {{ by("code") }}</h2>
<div class="box">
  <p>Sections marked "written by AI" were drafted by <b>{{ meta.model }}</b> ({{ meta.provider }}) on {{ meta.date }} with prompt v{{ meta.prompt_version }} (sha256 <code>{{ meta.prompt_sha256 }}</code>), in {{ meta.attempts }} attempt(s), at a cost of {{ meta.cost_usd|usd_appendix }} (GO <code>{{ meta.go_token }}</code>). Template sha256 <code>{{ template_sha256 }}</code>.</p>
  <p>The AI saw a code-built summary of frozen evidence (no attack payloads) and wrote prose with placeholders only. Code checked every placeholder and reference (grounding check: {{ "passed" if ground.ok else "FAILED" }}, {{ ground.stats.placeholders }} placeholders, {{ ground.stats.findings }} findings), filled in every number, and set every confidence level. People review the text and make the decision.</p>
  <p class="muted">Decision references (project records, for auditors): confidence rules {{ summary.confidence_rules }} and its amendments; analyst model and inputs D53; analysis, not recommendation D54 (as amended: the presenter decides in the demo); rendering D56; report structure D57; free-play audit timing D52; open-definition instability D42.</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Figure</th><th>Identifier</th><th>Value (full precision)</th></tr>
    {% for r in results %}<tr><td>{{ r.f.label }}</td><td><code>{{ r.key }}</code></td><td>{{ r.text if r.f.kind != "usd" else (r.f.value|usd_appendix) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </table>
</div>

<h2>Appendix C. Glossary {{ by("code") }}</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Known attack types</td><td>The three attack types the default defender is told about: SQL injection (CWE-89), cross-site scripting (CWE-79) and path traversal (CWE-22).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Default defender / original Blue</td><td>The defender as deployed in every match: it labels requests as one of the known attack types or as benign.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Open-definition defender / open Blue</td><td>The same defender with a wider attack definition (any attack), run afterwards on the same recorded traffic, for analysis only.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Free-play</td><td>Matches in which the attacker could try any technique, not only the known attack types.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Succeeded / successful attack</td><td>An attack request that solved one of the test application's built-in challenges.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Checked (audited)</td><td>The designer reviewed Red's attack labels, or judged whether each free-play request was an attack attempt; unchecked figures rest on Red's own labels.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>False alarm</td><td>A normal (non-attack) request the defender flagged as an attack.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Held-back normal requests</td><td>Normal requests set aside before any experiment and never used to build or tune anything.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Rule library</td><td>Detection rules the defender wrote in earlier training matches and reuses read-only; a request a rule answers needs no AI call.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>95% interval</td><td>The range of rates compatible with the observed counts (exact binomial interval); small samples give wide intervals.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Percentage points</td><td>The difference between two percentages (e.g. from 60.0% to 70.0% is +10.0 percentage points).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Confidence (High / Moderate / Low)</td><td>Set by code from fixed rules: checked figures with at least twenty units High, fewer Moderate; unchecked labels Low; the open-definition defender at most Moderate. A finding takes the lowest confidence of its figures.</td></tr>
</table>
{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
